-- Create the scratch BOX that data/transform/geometry cases mutate, then
-- db8000_scratch_delete.mac removes at the end of the recording.
--
-- Why a scratch element instead of mutating /1-LNR-Q005-PJ directly: a correct
-- restore leg has to put the element back to its *exact* prior values, and we
-- cannot know a production element's current POS/XLEN offline. Creating our own
-- element makes every before/after value self-determined, so the whole macro set
-- is writable (and reviewable) without an E3D probe run first.
--
-- Baseline it establishes, relied on by the restore legs downstream:
--   POS  E 0 N 0 U 0  (default for a fresh BOX under its owner)
--   XLEN 1000  YLEN 1000  ZLEN 1000
--
-- Destructive-by-design case: no restore leg (net = added). The element lives
-- until db8000_scratch_delete.mac, which is the last case in the manifest.

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/db8000_scratch_create.log" OVER
$P CODEX-DB8000-SCRATCH-CREATE-ALIVE
/1-LNR-Q005-PJ
Q CE
Q REF
Q NAME
NEW BOX /CODEX_DB8000_SCRATCH
XLEN 1000
YLEN 1000
ZLEN 1000
Q CE
Q REF
Q NAME
Q OWNE
Q POS
Q XLEN
Q YLEN
Q ZLEN
SAVEWORK 'CODEX db8000 create scratch BOX /CODEX_DB8000_SCRATCH'
$P CODEX-DB8000-SCRATCH-CREATE-DONE
ALPHA LOG END
